+# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# BLASTI Desktop App — Environment Variables
+# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+# This file documents ALL environment variables used by the Electron desktop app.
+# Copy this to .env and fill in your values.
+#
+# NOTE: The desktop app is an Electron shell that loads the web app.
+# Most configuration comes from the web app it connects to.
+# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+# ─── CONNECTION (the one setting that matters for VPS deploys) ────────
+# The CLOUD ORIGIN the desktop app talks to for login, sync and realtime —
+# the machine that actually serves /api/* and /socket.io/* (apps/api, the
+# Hono server, usually behind a reverse proxy). The UI itself is always
+# served locally by the embedded local API, so this is the ONLY URL you
+# normally need to set.
+#
+# ⚠️ ORIGIN ONLY — NEVER append a path (this is the #1 misconfiguration):
+#   ✅ BLASTI_CLOUD_URL="http://203.0.113.227"        (raw IP, HTTP testing)
+#   ✅ BLASTI_CLOUD_URL="https://blasti.example.com"  (domain + HTTPS)
+#   ❌ BLASTI_CLOUD_URL="http://203.0.113.227/api"    → app probes
+#      /api/api/health → 404 → "cloud unreachable". The app appends
+#      /api/* ITSELF. (Newer builds auto-strip the suffix with a warning.)
+#
+# HOW .env IS LOADED (Electron does NOT read .env by itself — BLASTI does,
+# see load-env.js / main.js; first match wins, OS environment overrides):
+#   1. OS environment variables      (runtime override, advanced use)
+#   2. <install>\resources\.env      (packaged app — EDITABLE AFTER INSTALL
+#       without rebuilding, e.g.
